==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-a}}
* {{rhymes|ang|ɑ|s=1}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|ang|id=masculine|:inh|gmw-pro:*-ō<id:agent noun>}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-ō}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ô}}. Cognate with {{cog|goh|-o}}.

====Suffix==== 
{{ang-head|nounf|inflsuf=1|g=m}}

# {{ng|marks the masculine nominative singular of n-stems}}
#: {{uxi|ang|ācweorn'''a'''|squirrel}}
#: {{uxi|ang|fol'''a'''|foal}}
#: {{uxi|ang|drac'''a'''|dragon}}
#: {{uxi|ang|grīm'''a'''|mask}}
#: {{uxi|ang|heorr'''a'''|door hinge}}

====Suffix==== 
{{ang-head|adjf|inflsuf=1|g=m}}

# {{ng|marks the weak masculine nominative singular of adjectives, and the subsequent nominalised form}}
#: {{afex|ang|eald<t:old>|ealda<alt:(sē) ealda><t:(the/that) old; (the/that) old one/thing>}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-noun||m}}

# {{senseid|ang|agent noun}} {{ng|forms masculine agent nouns, usually from verbs}}
#: {{syn|ang|-end|-ere}}
#: {{afex|ang|ġiefan<t:to give>|ġiefa<t:giver>}}
#: {{afex|ang|dēman<t:to judge>|dēma<t:a judge>}}
#: {{afex|ang|cuman<t:to come>|cuma<t:guest>}}

=====Declension=====
{{ang-decl-noun-n-m|-}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ang}}
{{suffixsee|ang|id=agent noun}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|enm|-e}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ang|agent noun}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-ō}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ô}}.

====Suffix====
{{ang-adv}} {{tlb|ang|unproductive}}

# {{senseid|ang|adverbial}} {{ng|forms adverbs}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Though it was common in Proto-Germanic and Proto-West Germanic, in Old English this ending is restricted to only a few adverbs, among them {{m|ang|sōna||immediately}} and {{m|ang|ġeāra||long ago}}. The competing suffix {{m|ang|-e}} is much more common, along with {{m|ang|-līċe}}.

=====Derived terms=====
{{suffixsee|ang|id=adverbial}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|enm|-e}} {{gl|fossilised}}
** {{desc|en|-e}} {{gl|archaic}}

===Etymology 3===

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|nounf|inflsuf=1|g=mf}}

# {{ng|marks the {{lg|nominative}}, {{lg|accusative}}, and {{lg|genitive}} plural of ō-stem feminine nouns and u-stem masculine nouns}}
#: {{afex|ang|sunu<t:son>|suna<t:sons, sons'>}}
#: {{afex|ang|talu<t:tale>|tala<t:tales, tales'>}}

===Etymology 4===
{{etymid|ang|genitive plural}}
{{inh+|ang|gmw-pro|*-ō|id=genitive plural}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ǫ̂}}, from the {{der|ang|ine-pro|-}} genitive plural ending {{m|ine-pro|*-oHom}} as attached to thematic (''eh₂''-stem and ''o''-stem) nouns.

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|nounf|inflsuf=1|g=m,n}}

# {{ng|marks the {{lg|genitive}} plural of a-stem nouns}}
#: {{afex|ang|word<t:word>|worda<t:words'>}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|enm|-e|id=genitive plural}}

===Etymology 5===

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|nounf|inflsuf=1|g=mf}}

# {{ng|marks the {{lg|genitive}} and {{lg|dative}} singular of u-stem nouns}}
#: {{afex|ang|sunu<t:son>|suna<t:son's, son>}}

