Page 13 -aþ: -------- begin text --------
==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ang|-að}}
* {{alt|ang|-eþ}}
* {{alt|ang|-ᚨᚦ}} {{q|runic}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-aþ}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|ang|id=third-person singular|:inh|gmw-pro:*-ōþ<ety:inh<gem-pro:*-ōþi>>}}
{{inh+|ang|gmw-pro|*-ōþ}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ōþi}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ang|-as|-es||Northumbrian}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|verbf|inflsuf=1}}

# {{ng|marks the third person singular present indicative of class 2 weak verbs}}
#: {{uxi|ang|Hit mac'''aþ'''|it makes}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|enm|-eth|id=third-person singular}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ang|plural}}
{{inh+|ang|gmw-pro|*-anþ|t=third person plural indicative ending of weak verbs}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-anþi|t=third person plural indicative ending of weak verbs}}. Cognate with {{cog|osx|-ad}}, {{cog|swg|-ad}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ang|-as|-es||Northumbrian}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-head|verbf|inflsuf=1}}

# {{ng|marks the first, second and third person plural present indicative ending of strong verbs, class 1 weak verbs, and class 3 weak verbs}}
#: {{uxi|ang|Hīe cum'''aþ'''|they come}}
# {{lb|ang|used without postpositioned {{l|ang|ġē|"ġē"}}}} {{ng|marks the second person plural imperative ending of strong verbs, class 1 weak verbs, and class 3 weak verbs}}
#: {{uxi|ang|Cum'''aþ'''!|Come!}} {{gl|see usage note below}}

=====Usage notes=====
* '''''-aþ''''' is used to form the second person plural imperative form of verbs except when the verb is followed by the pronoun {{m|ang|ġē}}, in which case the verb takes '''{{m|ang|-e|id=second person plural imperative}}''' (e.g. ''cumaþ!'' ("come!") vs. ''cume ġē!'' ("come ye!")).

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ang|-iaþ}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|enm|-eth|id=plural}}

===Etymology 3===

====Suffix====
{{ang-noun||m}}

# {{alt form|ang|-oþ}}; {{ng|forms concrete nouns from verbs}}
