Page 52 -ere: -------- begin text --------
==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ang|-re||Late West Saxon}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|ang|:inh|id=agent suffix|gmw-pro:*-ārī<id:agent suffix>}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-ārī}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ārijaz}}.

Traditionally and still usually held to be from {{der|ang|la|-ārius}}. An alternative proposal from Gąsiorowski suggests that ''*-ārijaz'' is a native formation; he derives it from earlier ''*-azrijaz'', which he etymologises as a zero-grade form of {{m|ine-pro|*-sōr}} suffixed with {{m|ine-pro|*-ih₂}}, creating a suffix ''*-sr-ih₂'' for forming feminine agent nouns, which were then masculinised by attaching {{m|ine-pro|*-ós}}. He also suggests a relation to {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-astrijā}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|ofs|-ere}}, {{cog|osx|-āri}}, {{cog|goh|-āri}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-ere}}
* {{rhymes|ang|e.re|s=2}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-noun||m}}

# {{ng|forms masculine agent nouns, originally applied only to nouns}}
#: {{syn|ang|-a|-end}}
#: {{afex|ang|dōm<t:judgement>|dōmere<t:judge>}}
#: {{afex|ang|fugol<t:bird>|fuglere<t:fowler>}}

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-ja-m|-er}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ang}}

====Descendants====
* {{desctree|enm|-ere|id=agent suffix}}

