==Old English==

===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|ang|id=adjectives|:inh|gmw-pro:*-g<id:adjectives>|tree=+}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-g|*-ag, -ig}}. Still distinct in the earliest texts.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alt|ang|-iċ|-eġ}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ang-IPA|-iġ}}
* {{rhymes|ang|ij|s=1}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-adj|-iġ}}

# {{l|en|-y}}; {{ng|forms adjectives from nouns and verbs}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The variant form ''-eġ'' (or ''-eg'') often occurs specifically when followed by suffixes containing back vowels. Ringe and Taylor (2014) suggest that prehistoric ''*-ag'' failed to fully raise to ''-iġ'' in this environment, with the variant reflecting a preserved transitional form.<ref>{{R:ang:DOE|page=335}}</ref>

=====Declension=====
{{ang-adecl|-iġ}}

