==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ang|-ysċ}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-isċ}}

===Etymology 1===
{{dercat|ang|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-isk}}.
{{etymon|ang|id=-ish|:inh|gmw-pro:*-isk<id:adjective>}}

====Suffix====
{{ang-adj|-isċ}}

# [[-ish]]; {{ng|forms {{lg|relational}} adjectives, i.e. adjectives meaning “of or relating to”, from nouns and proper nouns}}
#: {{afex|ang|ċild<t:child>|ċildisċ<t:childish>}}
#: {{afex|ang|ielf<t:elf>|ielfisċ<t:elvish>}}
#: {{afex|ang|man<t:person>|mennisċ<t:human>}}
#: {{afex|ang|þēod<t:nation>|þēodisċ<t:national>}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Replaces {{ncog|la|-icus}} in loanwords.
* Almost the only suffix used to form demonym adjectives, i.e. those meaning "of some ethnic group or nationality": {{m|ang|Frīsa||a Frisian}} → {{m|ang|Frīsisċ||Frisian}}. Other examples include {{m|ang|Āfricānisċ||African}}, {{m|ang|Arabisċ||Arabian}}, {{m|ang|Assirisċ||Assyrian}}, {{m|ang|Brettisċ||British}}, {{m|ang|Centisċ||Kentish}}, {{m|ang|Crēċisċ||Greek}}, {{m|ang|Denisċ||Danish}}, {{m|ang|Egyptisċ||Egyptian}}, {{m|ang|Englisċ||English}}, {{m|ang|Frenċisċ||French/Frankish}}, {{m|ang|Gotisċ||Gothic}}, {{m|ang|Indisċ||Indian}}, {{m|ang|Iūdēisċ||Jewish}}, {{m|ang|Ispānisċ||Spanish}}, {{m|ang|Isrāēlisċ||Israelite}}, {{m|ang|Langbeardisċ||Lombardic}}, {{m|ang|Mæcedonisċ||Macedonian}}, {{m|ang|Mierċisċ||Mercian}}, {{m|ang|Norþanhymbrisċ||Northumbrian}}, {{m|ang|Persisċ||Persian}}, {{m|ang|Pihtisċ||Pictish}}, {{m|ang|Rōmānisċ||Roman}}, {{m|ang|Samaritānisċ||Samaritan}}, {{m|ang|Sċyttisċ||Scottish}}, {{m|ang|*Seaxisċ||Saxon}}, {{m|ang|Sicilisċ||Sicilian}}, {{m|ang|Syrisċ||Syrian}}, {{m|ang|Syrofēnisċ||Syrophoenician}}, {{m|ang|Troiānisċ||Trojan}}, and {{m|ang|wīelisċ||Welsh}}. The word for "Ethiopian," {{m|ang|Siġelhearwen}}, is a rare exception to this pattern.

=====Declension=====
{{ang-adecl|-isċ}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|enm|-ish|-isch}}
** {{desc|sco|-is}}
** {{desc|en|-ish}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-iską}}, {{m|gem-pro|*-iskiją}}.

