===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ang|-an|id=-um||late, confused}}
* {{alt|ang|-ū||scribal abbreviation}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-um}}, possibly from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-amaz}} with reduction and analogical zero-grade, ultimately from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*-mos}}, the dative-ablative plural ending. Cognate to modern {{cog|de|-en}} and {{cog|pl|-om}}.

===Suffix===
{{ang-head|nounf|addlpos=adjf|inflsuf=1}}

# {{ng|forms the dative plural of essentially all nouns}}
#: {{afex|ang|hund<t:dog>|hundum<t:dogs>}}
#: {{afex|ang|sċip<t:ship>|sċipum<t:ships>}}
# {{ng|forms the strong and weak dative and instrumental plural of adjectives}}
# {{ng|forms the strong dative singular of masculine and neuter adjectives}}

====Usage notes====
* The abbreviated form ''-ū'' is used inconsistently in writing, even within the same text; for example, line 5 of ''{{w|Beowulf}}'' includes the text {{m|ang|monegum|monegū}} {{m|ang|mægþum}}, which contains both the abbreviated and unabbreviated forms

====Descendants====
* {{desc|enm|-en|id=dative plural|qq=early, through the variant {{m|ang|-an|id=-um}}|alts=1}}

