{{etymon|ang|id=gerund noun|:inh|gem-pro:*-ungō<id:noun suffix>}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-ungu}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-ungō}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|osx|-unga}} ({{cog|nds|-inge}}, {{m|nds|-ing}}), {{cog|odt|-inga}}, {{m|odt|-unga}} ({{cog|nl|-ing}}), {{cog|goh|-unga}} ({{cog|de|-ung}}), {{cog|non|-ung}}, {{m|non|-ing}} ({{cog|sv|-ing}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-ung}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-noun||f}}

# {{ng|forms nouns from verbs, denoting verbal action or an instance of it; or denoting a substance involved in the verbal action}}

====Usage notes====
* In general, '''''-ung''''' is used with class Ia and II weak verbs, {{m|ang|-ing}} with all other verbs. 

====Declension====
{{ang-decl-noun-o-f|-ung}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ang}}

====Descendants====
* {{desctree|enm|-ynge}}
-------- end text --------
Page 219 -ung: Skipped, no changes
Page 220 -unga: -------- begin text --------
==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ang|-inga|-enga|-onga|-ningas|-nunges}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|ang|-ung}}, noun suffix + {{m|ang|-a}}, adverbial suffix.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|-un+ga}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-adv}}

# {{ng|forms adverbs from nouns (originally verbal nouns), verbs, adjectives, pronouns and prepositions}}
#: {{af|ang|fǣr<t:sudden danger, peril>|[[færinga]], [[fǣrunga]]<t:suddenly>}}
#: {{af|ang|wēn<t:belief, hope, expectation; probability>|[[wēnunga]], [[wēninga]]<t:possibly, perhaps, by chance>}}
#: {{af|ang|healf<t:half>|healfunga<t:by halves, partially, to some extent, imperfectly>}}
#: {{af|ang|hōlian<t:to oppress, to slander>|[[hōlinga]], [[hōlunga]]<t:in vain, without reason>}}
#: {{af|ang|full<t:full>|fullunga<t:fully>}}
#: {{af|ang|*dearnian<to conceal, to hide>|dearnunga<t:secretly, privately, latently>}}
#: {{af|ang|[[hwæthwugu]], [[hwæthwegu]], [[hwæthugu]]<t:somewhat; something>|[[hwæthwegununges]], [[hwæthuguningas]]<t:somewhat>}}
#: {{af|ang|ġeġn<t:again>|[[ġeġnunga]], [[ġeġninga]]<t:immediately, directly>}}

====Usage notes====
* ''-unga'' is properly the suffix used with Class 2 Weak verbs, and ''-inga'' with all others. The distinction is frequently blurred, and forms exist that do not adhere to the original rule.

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ang}}

