Page 232 -wintre: -------- begin text --------
==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*-wintrī}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*-wintruz}}. Cognate with {{cog|non|-vetr}} and {{cog|got|-𐍅𐌹𐌽𐍄𐍂𐌿𐍃}}. Equivalent to {{suf|ang|winter|e|id2=adjectival}}. Compare the [[w:German language|German]] suffix {{m|de|-jährig}}, of similar form and meaning.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|wintre}}

===Suffix===
{{ang-adj}}

# {{ng|forms adjectives meaning “year(s) old”}}; -[[year]]-[[old]]
#* '''c. 893''', [[w:Alfred the Great|King Alfred's]] ''[[w:Doom Book|Laws]]''
#*: {{quote|ang|Tīen'''wintre''' cniht mæġ bēon þīefþe ġewita.|A ten'''-year-old''' boy can be an accessory to a theft.}}
#* '''late 9th century''', ''[https://www.helsinkicorpus.arts.gla.ac.uk/browse.py?fs=100&format=html&highlight=&pb=true&params=false&toc=author&pln=false&text=mart The Old English Martyrology]''
#*: {{quote|ang|Sanctus Iūstus wæs eahta'''wintre''' þā hē martyrdōm þrōwode for Criste.|Saint Justus was eight '''years old''' when he became a martyr for Christ.}}
#* '''c. 1020''', [[w:Wulfstan of York|Wulfstan]], [[w:Cnut the Great|King Cnut's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=KBvfHW3H5WMC&newbks=0&pg=PA324 second law code]
#*: {{quote|ang|Wē willaþ þæt ǣlċ mann ofer twelf'''wintre''' selle þone āþ þæt hē nylle þēof bēon ne þēofes ġewita.|We want everyone over twelve '''years old''' to give an oath that they will not be a thief or a thief's accomplice.}}
#* '''c. 935''', [[w:Æthelstan|King Æthelstan's]] [https://books.google.com/books?id=_b1czbLGvqYC&pg=PA168 sixth law code]
#*: {{quote|ang|Ne slēa man nānne ġingran mann þonne fiftīene'''winterne''' mann, būtan hē hine werian wille oþþe flēo and on hand gān nylle.|No one should be executed who is younger than a fifteen-'''year-old''', unless they resist arrest [lit. ''try to defend themselves''] or try to escape and refuse to give themselves up.}}
#* '''late 9th century''', [https://books.google.com/books?id=xtM0rOEXqJIC&pg=PA89 translation] of [[w:Orosius|Orosius’]] ''History Against the Pagans''
#*: {{quote|ang|Hannibal ġecȳðde þone nīþ and þone hete þe hē beforan his fæder ġeswōr þā hē nigon'''wintre''' cniht wæs þæt hē nǣfre ne wurde Rōmāna frēond.|Hannibal showed the hatred and the malice that he felt when he swore before his father as a nine-'''year-old''' boy that he would never become a friend of the Romans.}}
#* '''late 9th century''', [https://books.google.com/books?id=xtM0rOEXqJIC&pg=PA91 translation] of [[w:Orosius|Orosius’]] ''History Against the Pagans''
#*: {{quote|ang|Æfter þām hīe ġesetton tictātor þæt hē sċolde bēon hearra ofer þā consulas, sē wæs hāten Decius Iūnius. Hē næs būtan seofontīene'''wintre'''.|After that, they chose a dictator to rule over the consuls, whose name was Decius Junius. He was only seventeen '''years old'''.}}
# {{ng|forms adjectives meaning “lasting a specific number of years”}}; -[[year]]
#* '''late 9th century''', [https://books.google.com/books?id=xtM0rOEXqJIC&pg=PA126 translation] of [[w:Orosius|Orosius’]] ''History Against the Pagans''
#*: {{quote|ang|Dioclētiānus and Maximiānus bebudon ēhtnesse cristenra manna—Dioclētiānus ēastane and Maximiānus westane—and for þām bebode wurdon fela martyra on tīen'''wintrum''' fierste.|Diocletian and Maximian ordered the persecution of Christians—Diocletian from the east and Maximian from the west—and because of that order there were many martyrs in a ten-'''year''' period.}}

====Usage notes====
* Often written as a separate word in modern transcriptions, but {{m|ang|twiwintre||two years old}} and {{m|ang|þriwintre||three years old}}, with the prefix forms of "two" and "three," show that ''-wintre'' was a suffix.

====Declension====
{{ang-adecl|-wintre}}

====Derived terms====
{{suffixsee|ang}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|enm|-winter}}

====See also====
* {{l|ang|-nihte}}
-------- end text --------
